LobsterAI patch (no upstream equivalent as of 2026-11): read the Windows
install roots and the console code page without starting child processes.

v2026.8.1 resolves trusted System32 paths from HKLM by running reg.exe four
times, and finds the console code page by running `cmd.exe /d /s /c chcp`.
Both run synchronously right after the gateway reports ready (~470 ms
together), and non-Microsoft processes starting reg.exe/cmd.exe trip common
EDR heuristics. Read the same HKLM values through koffi and
advapi32!RegGetValueW (64-bit view, then default view, reg.exe text form),
and the code page through kernel32 (GetConsoleOutputCP when a console is
attached, else the HKCU\Console CodePage override or GetOEMCP, which is what
the new console chcp ran in reported). Environment variables stay untrusted
for these roots. reg.exe and chcp remain the fallback when the native helper
cannot answer. Retire when upstream reads these values natively.

